{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>To listen to Balaam</b> — and adjacent to it is <b>you shall not seek their peace</b>. As stated in HaNezikin 40b. And adjacent is <b>you shall not abominate the Edomite</b>, to say: even though it is written <b>Esau hated Jacob</b>, <b>you shall not abominate the Edomite</b>. For the Ammonites did not greet you with bread and water, but he greeted you, as it is said: <b>as the children of Esau did to me</b>."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:25.760731549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}